    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d474-a3">

                <pb facs="1034" n="938" xml:id="pg938"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 148.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Mr.
                            Silvela.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-12-27"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 27,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    reception of your excellency’s note of yesterday authorizing (should it be
                    necessary) the passage over Spanish soil of a criminal now under arrest at
                    Lisbon.</p>
                <p>I beg to assure your excellency that this prompt act of international comity
                    cannot fail to be warmly reciprocated by the government I have the honor to
                    represent.</p>
                <p>I directed the officer who is to take charge of the criminal to notify me by
                    telegram of the route he intended to follow, and shall hasten to inform your
                    excellency thereof, in compliance with your request.</p>
                <p>I gladly avail myself, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
